# The interactive site under docs/ is hand-authored presentation and data code.
#
# It is NOT ignored to dodge formatting - it is ignored because reformatting it
# destroys things prettier has no way to understand:
#
#   app.js      - template literals with hand-placed newlines that line up quiz
#                 options and mock-exam chrome. Prettier reflows them and the
#                 rendered HTML whitespace shifts.
#   style.css   - one declaration per line, grouped by visual layer. Prettier
#                 collapses it to as few lines as possible, which defeats the
#                 grouping and makes the diff for a real style change unreadable.
#   curriculum.js / answers.js - large curated data literals (100KB+). A prettier
#                 pass produces a 10,000-line diff for a one-line content fix.
#
# These files are still checked, just by the tool that suits them:
#   npm run check:syntax      (node --check on the authored data)
#   npm run site:check        (build/site.mjs --check: curriculum/answers schema,
#                              exercise id cross-references and generated-file freshness)
#
# docs/index.html is small and hand-authored, but it is excluded with the rest of
# docs/ so the shell and the generated data cannot drift into a formatting fight.
docs/

# Generated: docs/assets/guides/ and docs/assets/answers/ are rewritten wholesale
# by `node build/site.mjs`. Formatting them separately would fight the build.